WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.517
This page summarizes your required Module 3 work.

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:08.267
The module tracks ten knowledge checks and six coding exercises.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:12.222
Before selecting Complete Module, review the counters.

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:17.912
If something is incomplete, use the progress information to return to the relevant slide.

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:23.552
When you select Complete Module, the page creates an Assignment 3 submission summary containing your

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:30.292
completion status, knowledge-check answers, and the SQL saved for the coding exercises.

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:33.712
Review that summary before copying it to Canvas.

00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:39.347
If the module is incomplete, the page will warn you before you copy the current progress.

00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:42.562
Your progress is stored locally in this browser.

00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:49.917
Changing devices, clearing browser storage, or using a private window may not carry the saved work with you.

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:54.872
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:54.872 --> 00:01:01.152
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:03.622
and the shape of the expected output.

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:09.142
In a real setting such as an application safely inserting or updating business records,

00:01:09.142 --> 00:01:15.302
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:01:15.302 --> 00:01:17.562
before discussing syntax.

00:01:17.562 --> 00:01:23.940
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
